/-!
# Local steps toward the empty-family commuting-Sylow dichotomy

The non-Sylow-centralizing case supplies a distinct commuting conjugate by
normalizer growth. The odd-intersection argument identifies the product as z
once the D₈ conjugation identity has been constructed, and yields the exact
conjugacy-centralizer intersection from a uniform construction.

The quotient interfaces distinguish the full fixed group from the image of
the original centralizer. An index-two image cannot have a perfect overgroup.
The A₆ exception, invariant subgroup of order four, quotient index and missing
involution, and the two actual model exclusions remain assembly obligations.
This module does not yet assert `CommutingSylowDichotomy`.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of 16.4.9(2), printed p.1190, between (+) and (!).
-/
